# <Project> — Errors & Findings Registry

> **Purpose.** A durable, greppable record of every error, defect, and gotcha hit across
> this project, so a future session can (a) **recognize** a problem it has seen before
> from its *signature*, (b) **reuse** the known fix, and (c) **catch the whole class
> upfront** via the listed guard.
>
> **How to use this file.**
> - Hit an error? **Grep the registry (this hub + `errors/*.md`) for the error string or
>   symptom first** — most are already here with a fix.
> - Before any build / deploy / migration, skim **Part 1 (Recurring Failure Classes)**.
> - Concrete incidents are split per area under `errors/` (see the Index). Each entry
>   leads with a *Signature* (an actual error string or observable behavior) so it's
>   greppable — and machine-matchable by any triage tooling.
> - Adding a finding? Append it to the right `errors/<area>.md` section in the entry
>   format: **ID — Title · Signature · Cause · Fix · Guard · Status · Source**. If it's a
>   new pattern that has bitten more than once, add a `PAT-` class here too.
> - `Status: FIXED` = resolved in code/config. `Status: OPEN` = unresolved; the live open
>   set is rolled up in **Part 3**.
>
> **Layout note.** This hub holds Part 1 (recurring `PAT-*` classes) and Part 3 (the
> open-items rollup). The per-incident detail a "Part 2" would hold is externalized into
> `errors/<area>.md` — there is intentionally **no Part 2** section here.
>
> _Last full rebuild: <YYYY-MM-DD>._ (Incremental appends land continuously; this stamp
> marks the last full recompile, not the last edit.)

